Z||000013||artherd||10-20-2001||12:50 AM||||Why not use a Quad4 engine?  it's still a little cammy 4-banger, only it's good for 190HP (in w41 HO trim... careful, those are rather rare!)<P>That's just about 200bhp, and better mileage (bleh, that matters not to the Jedi!) than the crap-4 that's in the car now (I have one. correction, had one. It threw TWO connecting rods... &lt;explative deleted&gt; )<P>If you do try a Saturn engine (cool idea, they're incredibly like our cars, infact the saturn body pannel process and assembley, etc is basically Fiero-derived. pretty cool.) do go for the biggest one you can find...  <P>Hey, don't they have a 3-ish litre DOHC v6?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
