Z||000016||Tryxalon||10-21-2001||06:32 PM||||Sorry, Malacite, but you must be using the "Gross Vehicle Weight" on the Saturn Wagon. <P> A 2000 Saturn SW1 has a curb weight of 2,434 PER <A HREF="http://www.Saturn.com" TARGET=_blank>www.Saturn.com</A>  with the 1900cc 100hp/114fp SOHC4. <P>The 2000 Saturn SW2 has a curb weight of 2600 with a 135hp/122fp DOHC4. <P> The LW200 has a 135hp 140f/p 2300cc DOHC 4 at 3,070 <P>The 2002 LW300 has a 182/190 3.0 DOHC V6. <BR> <BR>My son has a 99 SC2 one, and we just did a few measurements. The 1900 DOHC 4 with transmission will fit ... but not with Fiero Mounts.  Saturn has four "cradle" mounts and a "head to body" mount that is on the serpentine belt side, but the Engine/Trans is a "powerplant module".  <P>It is a doable swap -- move the battery and fabricate the "nose" mount. Fabricate the two "floating frame members" to accom0date mounting the Saturn motor to -- and then the mount to mount the sub-frames to the cradle. <P>If you are using the Fiero Transmission - it looks like you will need an adapter. If you use the Saturn transmission (recomended -- see the mount for engines above) Then you will have to manufacture the Axle shafts. <P>IF you do all this, then the good thing is the wiring harness will reach to put the ECM inthe fiero location (make it easier to splice) and the Exhaust from the Saturn engine will only require a small (under the trunk to Exhaust pipe) costom exhaust -- others have done this before.  <P><BR>All in all?  Lot of work for little REAL change.  The SBC v-8 swap has GOT to be easier. But ... you may want a challenge!! <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||roadwarrior||10-21-2001||07:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by malacite:<BR><B>a four wheel drive fiero?<BR>what a concept. now if you used the drivetrain turned around, and mated it to a vw bug, or porsh 911 (twin turbo) mounted longitudally in the rear where the trunk should be...you could eat an impreza wrx, or any ricer for that matter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>i beleive i have strayed from the land of reality into the land of pipe dreams.<BR>besides. now that i've filled the console, engine compartment, front compartment and trunk with engine and drivetrain...where do i put my fuel tank?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>fuel tank goes where the passenger seat now sits either that or I could take a small pick-up like an s15 4*4 and modifie it enough to bolt a fiero body onto it, and heh there's nothing wronf with pipe dreams!<BR>||||reg||1
